<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="20886" href="schedule/2014/fall/LA/199/20886.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2014" href="schedule/2014.xml">2014</calendarYear><term id="120148" href="schedule/2014/fall.xml">Fall 2014</term><subject id="LA" href="schedule/2014/fall/LA.xml">Landscape Architecture</subject><course id="199" href="schedule/2014/fall/LA/199.xml">Undergraduate Open Seminar</course></parents><sectionNumber>MED</sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Landscape of Utopia</sectionTitle><creditHours>2 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Guides students on a tour of utopian landscapes in literature, film, popular media, and real places. From Teletubbies to the Simpsons; from News from Nowhere to The Hunger Games; from The Magical Mystery Tour to Blade Runner--landscapes depicted in our visions of the future offer clues to the "nature" of our hopes, our fears, and our ideals.  First Year Discovery Program Course.  Students should enroll in only one Discovery course.</sectionText><sectionDegreeAttributes>Discovery course.</sectionDegreeAttributes><sectionCappArea>Restricted to First Time Freshman students.</sectionCappArea><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>Open (Restricted)</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2014-08-25Z</startDate><endDate>2014-12-10Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LCD">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>04:00 PM</start><end>04:50 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>TR     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>18</roomNumber><buildingName>Temple Hoyne Buell Hall</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Deming" firstName="M">Deming, M</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>